      "claim": "The query SMILES corresponds to biperiden; no supplied L1-L6 card reports a direct oral bioavailability or matched oral/IV exposure measurement for biperiden, so no affirmative F < 20% evidence transfers to the query.",
      "card_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "C47, C59, and C62 report the same high Caco-2 permeability measurement for trihexyphenidyl (PappAB 46.29 ± 8.31 × 10^-6 cm/s, efflux ratio 0.22), a close structural analog sharing the phenyl/piperidine/tertiary-alcohol core with biperiden; this supports favorable intestinal absorption and no net gut-wall efflux, but is not a direct F measurement.",
      "card_ids": ["C47", "C59", "C62"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The physicochemical prior (logD 1.8, TPSA 23.47, MW 311) is favorable for absorption; the low neutral fraction and possible first-pass metabolism are caveats, not affirmative low-bioavailability evidence.",
      "card_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance and metabolic-stability records concern other molecules (loperamide, terfenadine, oxybutynin, fluphenazine, etc.) and do not provide biperiden-specific presystemic-loss evidence; for example, the oxybutynin CES1 record is not transferable because biperiden lacks the ester moiety.",
